.TH INZONECTL 1 "" "inzone-buds-mixer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inzonectl \- control the Sony INZONE Buds dongle audio routing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inzonectl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B inzonectl
selects and adjusts the native Game, Chat and Microphone endpoints that the
Sony INZONE Buds USB dongle (PC mode,
.BR 054c:0ec2 )
exposes through PipeWire. It talks to the PulseAudio\-compatible server with
.BR pactl (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the INZONE endpoints and the current defaults.
.TP
.B doctor
Show diagnostic information: versions, kernel, USB devices, cards, sinks and
sources. With
.BR \-\-report ,
the user, host and home directory names are masked and the text is wrapped in
a Markdown code block, ready to paste into a bug report.
.TP
.B profile
Activate the Pro Audio profile on the INZONE card.
.TP
.B game
Make Game the default output.
.TP
.B chat
Make Chat the default output.
.TP
.B mic
Make the INZONE microphone the default input.
.TP
.B default
Select the Game output and the INZONE microphone.
.TP
.BI "volume game|chat|mic " PERCENT
Set one endpoint's volume, 0 to 100.
.TP
.BI "balance " POSITION " \fR[\fIMAX\fR]"
Set the Game/Chat balance. 0 is Chat only, 50 is centered and 100 is Game
only.
.I MAX
is the highest volume either endpoint reaches, as a percentage; it defaults
to 50.
.TP
.BR version ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.B help
Show the command summary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PACTL
Path of the
.BR pactl (1)
command (default
.BR pactl ).
.TP
.B WPCTL
Path of the
.BR wpctl (1)
command (default
.BR wpctl ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/inzone-buds-mixer/config
Optional user configuration; see
.I config.example
in the documentation directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR inzone\-buds\-mixer (1),
.BR pactl (1),
.BR wpctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/RavenEibu/sony-inzone-buds-linux
